      "comment": "Disagree with the judge's own conclusion. The rationale is a self-refuting walkthrough: it opens claiming the skill got direct/indirect backwards, then investigates the actual persisted assertions three times over and ends with 'Upon review... this is correct... Re-examining... This is correct. The skill did not invent child->spouse relationships. The extraction is factually accurate and properly classified.' -- and then still scores it 1. Verified independently against this run's persisted assertions (a_009/a_018/a_027/a_035): all relationship assertions to the head of household are evidence_type 'direct', matching the 1900 census's explicit relationship column, exactly as the per-test doctrine requires. This test flipped from 3-for-3 pass to 2-for-2 fail exactly at the point main's #2200 landed (delegate-to-convert-dates change to record-extraction/SKILL.md) -- worth knowing that at least this occurrence is a judge-scoring artifact, not evidence #2200 broke relationship-classification behavior. Unrelated to issue #2021, but flagging since it bears on whether #2200 needs a look."
